@meta
id: 12-02
title: One search, every match
chapter: 12
type: lesson
skills: search-slash, search-next
par: 32
minutes: 4
vscode: Enter again in the find box, or F3
open: order.provider.test.ts

@brief
Somebody copied a test block and forgot to change the assertion. The
`ship` test sets the order up as submitted, ships it, and then asserts it
is still `PENDING`. It should assert `SHIPPED`.

The word `PENDING` appears five times in this file and four of them are
correct. You want the last one.

The point of the lesson is that a search is not one jump. Having typed a
pattern once, you own it: one key walks forward through every match in
the file, another walks back. Typing the same search again is a beginner
tell.

@keys
| `/text` `Enter` | forward to the next match |
| `n` | the next match of the same pattern |
| `N` | the previous match of the same pattern |

@hints
Search once for the word, then step through the matches until you are on
the one inside the `ship` test. Do not type the search a second time, and
do not count the matches before you start — just walk until you arrive.
--
`n` repeats the last search forward. `N` repeats it backward, which is
how you recover when you press `n` once too often.
--
`/PENDING` `Enter` puts you on the first one. Four presses of `n` put you
on the last. The cursor is then on the `P` of a word inside quotes, so
`ciw` and the right status finishes it.

@solution
/PENDING<Enter>  n n  ciwSHIPPED<Esc>  :wq<Enter>

`n` and `N` are the whole lesson. The search prompt is a cost you pay
once; after that, moving to the next occurrence is one keystroke, and it
costs the same whether the next occurrence is two lines away or nine
hundred.

Watch the bottom-right of the screen as you press `n`. Vim tells you
`search hit BOTTOM, continuing at TOP` when it wraps around the end of
the file. That message is useful: if you see it, you have been round the
whole file and every match has been visited.

The habit to build is *pattern first, refine with `n`*. Beginners type a
long precise search trying to land on exactly the right match. Fluent
users type a short sloppy one and press `n` a couple of times, because
`n` is cheaper than precision.

@start order.provider.test.ts
import { OrderProvider } from './order.provider';
import { stub, reveal } from 'jest-auto-stub';
import { OrderRepository } from './order.repository';
import { PaymentService } from '../../infrastructure/services/payment.service';
import { orderFactory } from '../../../test/factories/order.factory';

describe('OrderProvider', () => {
  const orderRepository = stub<OrderRepository>();
  const paymentService = stub<PaymentService>();
  const provider = new OrderProvider(orderRepository, paymentService);

  afterEach(() => {
    jest.resetAllMocks();
  });

  describe('create', () => {
    it('starts a new order as pending', async () => {
      const order = orderFactory({ status: 'PENDING' });
      reveal(orderRepository).create.mockResolvedValue(order);

      const result = await provider.create({ customerId: order.customerId, total: 500 });

      expect(result.status).toBe('PENDING');
    });
  });

  describe('addLine', () => {
    it('leaves a pending order pending', async () => {
      const order = orderFactory({ status: 'PENDING', total: 500 });
      reveal(orderRepository).findOne.mockResolvedValue(order);
      reveal(orderRepository).update.mockResolvedValue({ ...order, total: 800 });

      const result = await provider.addLine({ id: order.id, sku: 'SKU-19', price: 300 });

      expect(result.status).toBe('PENDING');
    });
  });

  describe('ship', () => {
    it('marks a submitted order as shipped', async () => {
      const order = orderFactory({ status: 'SUBMITTED' });
      reveal(orderRepository).findOne.mockResolvedValue(order);
      reveal(orderRepository).update.mockResolvedValue({ ...order, status: 'SHIPPED' });

      const result = await provider.ship({ id: order.id, carrier: 'DPD' });

      expect(result.status).toBe('PENDING');
    });
  });

  describe('cancel', () => {
    it('refunds and cancels', async () => {
      const order = orderFactory({ status: 'SUBMITTED' });
      reveal(orderRepository).findOne.mockResolvedValue(order);
      reveal(orderRepository).update.mockResolvedValue({ ...order, status: 'CANCELLED' });

      const result = await provider.cancel({ id: order.id });

      expect(paymentService.refund).toHaveBeenCalledWith(order.id);
      expect(result.status).toBe('CANCELLED');
    });
  });
});

@expected order.provider.test.ts
import { OrderProvider } from './order.provider';
import { stub, reveal } from 'jest-auto-stub';
import { OrderRepository } from './order.repository';
import { PaymentService } from '../../infrastructure/services/payment.service';
import { orderFactory } from '../../../test/factories/order.factory';

describe('OrderProvider', () => {
  const orderRepository = stub<OrderRepository>();
  const paymentService = stub<PaymentService>();
  const provider = new OrderProvider(orderRepository, paymentService);

  afterEach(() => {
    jest.resetAllMocks();
  });

  describe('create', () => {
    it('starts a new order as pending', async () => {
      const order = orderFactory({ status: 'PENDING' });
      reveal(orderRepository).create.mockResolvedValue(order);

      const result = await provider.create({ customerId: order.customerId, total: 500 });

      expect(result.status).toBe('PENDING');
    });
  });

  describe('addLine', () => {
    it('leaves a pending order pending', async () => {
      const order = orderFactory({ status: 'PENDING', total: 500 });
      reveal(orderRepository).findOne.mockResolvedValue(order);
      reveal(orderRepository).update.mockResolvedValue({ ...order, total: 800 });

      const result = await provider.addLine({ id: order.id, sku: 'SKU-19', price: 300 });

      expect(result.status).toBe('PENDING');
    });
  });

  describe('ship', () => {
    it('marks a submitted order as shipped', async () => {
      const order = orderFactory({ status: 'SUBMITTED' });
      reveal(orderRepository).findOne.mockResolvedValue(order);
      reveal(orderRepository).update.mockResolvedValue({ ...order, status: 'SHIPPED' });

      const result = await provider.ship({ id: order.id, carrier: 'DPD' });

      expect(result.status).toBe('SHIPPED');
    });
  });

  describe('cancel', () => {
    it('refunds and cancels', async () => {
      const order = orderFactory({ status: 'SUBMITTED' });
      reveal(orderRepository).findOne.mockResolvedValue(order);
      reveal(orderRepository).update.mockResolvedValue({ ...order, status: 'CANCELLED' });

      const result = await provider.cancel({ id: order.id });

      expect(paymentService.refund).toHaveBeenCalledWith(order.id);
      expect(result.status).toBe('CANCELLED');
    });
  });
});
